DISCOUNT AttnPacker's VAL CELL. Its released structures label
equivalent methyls arbitrarily, which HANDOFF already records as the
reason its re-scored row is not an audit. VAL chi1 is N-CA-CB-CG1, so
a CG1/CG2 swap moves it a full 120 degrees into a different well,
which is why that one cell reads worse than SCWRL's while every other
cell is the best in its row. LEU chi1 is N-CA-CB-CG and is untouched
by the same swap, so LEU is unaffected -- the two together are the
confirmation rather than a coincidence.

Reading it: ours is 22.7% overall, SER 43.7%, PHE 9.2%. If the
baselines show the same shape, the small polar types are the field's
hard case and our deficit is a uniform scaling of everyone's problem.
If they are flat across types where we are not, the shape is ours and
it points at a specific missing ingredient rather than at capacity.
